      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Observed TCP payload, sampled every 15 seconds.** Includes connections with local or remote port 4001/4002, IPv4 and IPv6, in the exporter network namespace. Outbound includes payload retransmissions; inbound uses kernel received bytes. Network headers and pure ACKs are excluded.\n\nCounters begin when collection starts. Connections that open and close between polls, and bytes after the final socket observation, can be missed. Range volumes are Prometheus estimates from observed counters, suitable for operations rather than billing. No data: enable `--per-peer-metrics` on Linux in the same network namespace as the node; allow at least two Prometheus scrapes for rates."
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.0.2"
    }
